{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795283582,"nonce":"fGVy5JfGbr+u4jagavdpIBPGK58=","message":"\u003e You should also include a fallback for devices without webGPU, with a warning about degraded graphical performance.\n\nThe owner decided on 2026-11-21: the game supports browsers without WebGPU.\n\n**Design.** One binary holds one backend, so the build makes two clients: one for WebGPU and one for WebGL2. The page asks the browser for a WebGPU adapter, and loads the WebGL2 client when it gets none. The menu then shows a warning that the graphics run slower. A later GPU simulation (issue 755cbcc) needs compute, which WebGL2 lacks, so it must switch off on the fallback.\n\nIssue 05f7390 builds the fallback with the client. This issue closes when a browser test shows a match on WebGL2.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}